Subject: address the configured forge in the behaviour-test harness

The behaviour suite's own forge calls name api.github.com directly:
e2etest.NewLiveClient builds gh.New(token) with no base URL, and the cleanup
and lock helpers send raw requests to https://api.github.com/... (five in
cleanup.go, one in testutil.go). The CLI under test already resolves its
forge from GITHUB_API_URL, so against an enterprise server or an emulator the
install lands on one forge while the harness creates, checks and deletes
slot repositories on another, with credentials not meant for it.

The harness now takes the API root from GITHUB_API_URL when it is set, and
api.github.com otherwise, for both the client and the raw requests. On an
Actions runner GITHUB_API_URL is already https://api.github.com, so hosted
runs are unchanged.

Gaps BT-H1 and BT-H2 of .ledger/plans/fullsend-behaviour-tests-plan.md.
These are host-assumption defects in their own right; whether they go
upstream as problem-only issues is the conformance campaign's decision.

Breadboard note: test-only. Nothing here is compiled into the fullsend
binary, so it is not in the build list in deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh;
the behaviour-test run applies it on top of that list.

diff --git a/internal/e2etest/apibase_test.go b/internal/e2etest/apibase_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..1415da3bb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/e2etest/apibase_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+package e2etest
+
+import (
+	"context"
+	"net/http"
+	"net/http/httptest"
+	"testing"
+	"time"
+
+	"github.com/stretchr/testify/assert"
+	"github.com/stretchr/testify/require"
+)
+
+func TestGitHubAPIBaseURL_DefaultsToGitHubCom(t *testing.T) {
+	t.Setenv("GITHUB_API_URL", "")
+	assert.Equal(t, "https://api.github.com", githubAPIBaseURL())
+	assert.Equal(t, "https://api.github.com", NewLiveClient("token").BaseURL())
+}
+
+func TestGitHubAPIBaseURL_HonoursGitHubAPIURL(t *testing.T) {
+	t.Setenv("GITHUB_API_URL", " https://github.example/api/v3/ ")
+	assert.Equal(t, "https://github.example/api/v3", githubAPIBaseURL())
+	assert.Equal(t, "https://github.example/api/v3", NewLiveClient("token").BaseURL())
+}
+
+// The harness's raw REST calls follow GITHUB_API_URL too, not only the
+// forge client.
+func TestRawRequestsUseGitHubAPIURL(t *testing.T) {
+	var gotPath, gotAuth string
+	server := httptest.NewServer(http.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
+		gotPath, gotAuth = r.URL.Path, r.Header.Get("Authorization")
+		w.Header().Set("Content-Type", "application/json")
+		_, _ = w.Write([]byte(`{"created_at":"2026-11-07T12:00:00Z"}`))
+	}))
+	defer server.Close()
+	t.Setenv("GITHUB_API_URL", server.URL+"/api/v3")
+
+	created, err := getRepoCreatedAt(context.Background(), "token", "org", "repo")
+	require.NoError(t, err)
+	assert.Equal(t, "/api/v3/repos/org/repo", gotPath)
+	assert.Equal(t, "Bearer token", gotAuth)
+	assert.True(t, created.Equal(time.Date(2026, 11, 7, 12, 0, 0, 0, time.UTC)))
+}
